- dropdown-menu: render a `<DropdownMenu.Root><DropdownMenu.Trigger ref={handleRef}><button/></DropdownMenu.Trigger><DropdownMenu.Content/></Root>`, click to open, click to close → handleRef is called only once. Before the fix: open/close triggers re-renders → ref re-invocation (null+node on each commit). Wait — does the trigger re-render on open? The `DropdownMenu` root holds the `open` state and passes `context.open` to the trigger → yes, the trigger re-renders on open/close.
  Note: opening the menu also renders the content — no problem in jsdom.
- menu: submenu — render Menu.Root > Menu.Trigger > Menu.Content > Menu.Item with Menu.Sub? Actually MenuSubTrigger is inside a submenu: Menu.Root > Menu.Trigger (open) > Menu.Content > Menu.Sub > Menu.SubTrigger ref=... > Menu.SubContent. To make the SubTrigger re-render, the sub's open state changes. This is a bit heavier: need to open the root menu, then the sub. With fireEvent hover (pointermove) — Radix's menu uses pointer events + timers (the 100ms open timer via openTimerRef in MenuSubTrigger's onPointerMove!). Timers — need fake timers, or just render a sub-trigger in an open state... hmm, the sub's `context.open` — re-rendering the SubTrigger requires the sub's open to change. Alternative: force a re-render of the sub trigger via a parent state change? The sub trigger re-renders when Menu.Sub re-renders (context value changes?). Hmm — a simpler, more deterministic approach: don't rely on opening the sub, instead check the ref churn via re-renders... but if the sub never opens, does the sub trigger re-render at all?

